{
  "_about": "The workshops behind each merchant (build 51). Recipes never change. Times are in hours. Trinket and part recipes name junk materials from items.json (loot): a trinket takes one rare, one uncommon and the rest common; a part takes five, two of them rare. Build 53: Every trinket gives two stats, its major line first and its minor line second. A trinket has no name of its own: every stat has a first name and a second name (trinketWords), and a trinket is called by its major stat's first name and its minor stat's second name, after its rarity: Ember Immunity then Fire Resistance is a \"Cooling Body Fan\", so Fire then Ember and Ember then Fire are two different trinkets. Its rarity is rolled when the order is picked up (armory.trinketRarity: the chances of common, uncommon, rare and legendary for each tier of recipe), and the numbers in its recipe are the common ones: armory.trinketScale multiplies them for the rarer ones (an immunity is on or off). A trinket fits on any piece of gear or armor, one to a piece.",
